<!--
  COLLECTION track row, trailing action glyph.

  Frozen canonical: `Track Item N` > `Container` > `Button` > `Container` >
  `arrow_forward`, light nodes 2409:31572 / 31560 / 31542, dark 2444:18398 /
  18410 / 18422. The instance is 24x24 and carries rotation 45, inside a 33.94
  wrapper - 24 * sqrt(2), the bounding box of a 24 square turned through 45
  degrees.

  ## This is the exported vector, not an identification of it

  It used to be an identification, and that was the problem. The canonical
  snapshot records every node's box and none of its geometry (see
  tools/figma-export/nav-icons/README.md), so this file was previously authored
  from a Material glyph whose bounding box matched the canonical 16x16 at (4,4)
  on all four edges. That was enough to place the family and NOT enough to fix
  the path: measured against the real export afterwards, eight of the nine
  vertices agreed to 7e-5 and the ninth was out by 0.025, because the published
  Material Symbols path rounds one vertex to `10.6` where the authoritative
  drawing is symmetric at `10.575`. A matching box is not a matching path.

  So the geometry below is the owner's export from the frozen 3.6.6 Figma file,
  `tools/figma-export/collection-icons/owner-final/collection_row_action_arrow.svg`,
  copied verbatim - the same route the authoritative nav and player icons took.
  Nothing here is derived, rounded or re-drawn.

  ## Why the viewport is 40 and there is no rotation group

  The export is the whole control at 40x40: the ring, and the glyph already in
  its final north-east orientation. Taking the path as exported means taking its
  coordinate system as exported, so this vector is 40 and the 45 degrees are
  baked into the numbers rather than re-applied by a group. Re-deriving a
  24-space path to keep the old shape of the file would have meant transforming
  the authoritative geometry, which is the one thing this file must not do.

  Nothing moves. The ImageView is 40dp with `scaleType="center"`, so a 40dp
  drawable lands 1:1 where a 24dp one was centred in it, and the ink is in the
  same place either way:

    before   24 viewport, ink 5.636..17.657, centred in 40  =  13.636..25.657
    after    40 viewport, ink 13.636..25.657                =  13.636..25.657

  identical on both axes, which `CollectionRowActionGlyphTest` asserts against
  the export's own coordinates rather than assumes.

  ## What is deliberately NOT taken from the export

  The rect. The export carries the ring because Figma exports the control, and
  the ring already exists as `bg_collection_row_action.xml` - which the export
  confirms exactly: `x/y 1`, 38 square, `rx 19`, `stroke 2`, `#1C4771` is an
  oval with a 2px INSIDE stroke on `primary` at 40. Folding it in here would
  duplicate it and cost the ring its own themed colour.

  The fill. `#1C4771` is `primary` in the light theme; the view supplies it
  through `app:tint="@color/primary"`, which is what gives the dark theme its
  own `#5FD9B4`. The white below is a placeholder an untinted preview shows and
  nothing draws.
-->
